    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ)_\n\n## What\n\nCUA is gone on every system, and the Emacs defaults for the same jobs are unbound, so there is one layer of keys.\n\n- **Mac (Command = Super):** `s-c` copy, `s-x` cut, `s-v` paste, `s-z` undo, `s-Z` and `S-s-z` redo (the latter is the event Emacs usually gets for Command+Shift+Z).\n- **Linux and Windows (Ctrl):** `C-S-c` copy, `C-S-x` cut, `C-v` paste, `C-z` undo, `C-S-z` redo.\n- **Unbound everywhere:** `C-y`, `C-w`, `M-w`, `C-_`, `C-/`, `C-?`, `C-M-_`, `C-x u`.\n- `sp-text-manipulation.org` documents it, including a caveats list for unbinding `C-w`/`M-w`/`C-y`. `sp-keys.org` no longer says CUA is on. The `.el` is the tangled copy.\n\n## Readings I chose\n\n- Without CUA, plain `C-c` and `C-x` must stay prefixes, so copy and cut on Linux/Windows use the Shift variants. Say if you would rather have something else.\n- Redo is the built-in `undo-redo`, not undo-tree.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container); please try on the Mac and on Linux/Windows.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAZg8pR9NBT6MCe97U\n",
